@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It is useful when you want raw text output.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text to the console width, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. Output still goes through the usual print pipeline, so render hooks, buffering and capture work as they do for print.
+
+By default ``out`` applies highlighting (``highlight=True``), even if the console was created with highlighting disabled. Pass ``highlight=None`` to use the console setting, or ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off. The ``style`` argument accepts a style name or :class:`~rich.style.Style` object and is applied as print applies it.
+
+    >>> console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+
